/* Bhasaly - Religious studies content, UZBEK (uz).
   Translated from faith/ne.js. The English [2] and the scripture reference [3]
   of every paragraph are byte-identical to the Nepali source; only the native
   [0] and the romanization [1] are Uzbek.

   Vocabulary follows the Uzbek Bible (Muqaddas Kitob), verified against its
   Mark and John text: Xudo God, Iso Jesus, Rabbiy Lord, Oʻgʻli Son, gunoh
   sin, najot salvation, qutqarmoq to rescue, Muqaddas Ruh Holy Spirit,
   Xudoning Shohligi the kingdom of God, Xushxabar gospel, xoch cross, ahd
   covenant, paygʻambar prophet, shogird disciple, qurbonlik sacrifice,
   maʼbad temple, Qoʻzi lamb, imon keltirmoq to believe, abadiy hayot
   eternal life. NOTE the contrast with Urdu: there Christians deliberately
   avoid the Muslim form Isa, but the Uzbek Bible itself uses ISO, so that is
   what this pack uses. Respect is carried by capitalising divine pronouns
   (U, Oʻz, Oʻzi), which is what the Uzbek Bible does - there is no royal-verb
   system as in Khmer or Lao.

   SCRIPT HAZARD: Uzbek Latin needs U+02BB MODIFIER LETTER TURNED COMMA for
   oʻ / gʻ and U+02BC MODIFIER LETTER APOSTROPHE for the tutuq belgisi. An
   ASCII apostrophe would break the inline onclick handlers, and a Cyrillic
   lookalike (а с о и г) is invisible on review - the generator asserts
   against both.

   Romanization follows lang/uz.js: it is a PRONUNCIATION respelling, not a
   transliteration - x->kh, oʻ->aw, gʻ->gh, and the tutuq belgisi is dropped
   (baʼzan -> bazan). Paraphrase only - never copied translation text.
   The two Nepal references in the source are localised to Uzbekistan
   (the abraham note and newcreation para 4). */

